EAT(1)                      General Commands Manual                     EAT(1)

NAME
       eat - a syntax-highlighting cat

SYNOPSIS
       eat [OPTIONS] [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       eat prints the highlighted contents of FILEs. See also cat(1) and
       printf(3p) for related tools.

OPTIONS
       -A, --show-all
              Show non-printable characters.

       -l, --language <LANG>
              Override syntax detection.

       -p, --plain
              Disable highlighting and decorations.

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
       EAT_PAGER
              The pager binary; falls back to $PAGER, then less.

EXAMPLES
       eat -l rust src/main.rs
       printf 'hello' | eat -l shellscript

SEE ALSO
       bat(1), cat(1), less(1)
